 "literal": "Not departing if there is, to me tell; otherwise, your quick return, to those who survive, tell.",
 "translation": "If you are not departing, tell me; but as for your quick return, tell that to those who will survive until then.",
 "modern": "நீ போகாமல் இருக்கப் போகிறாய் என்றால் அதை என்னிடம் சொல்; மாறாக, நீ சீக்கிரம் திரும்பி வருவதைப் பற்றி, நீ இல்லாத காலத்தில் உயிர் பிழைத்திருப்பவர்களிடம் சொல்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine speaks to her departing lover, unable to bear the grief of separation. She tells him that if he has decided not to leave, he should tell her that happy news. However, if he is indeed leaving and promises a quick return, he should tell that to those who can survive the grief of separation; she herself will not survive to hear of his return.",
